-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4e91524afa2694dc9267932e556e0313273ba5f3dbbb3d2c3252f64e535d590f","event_uuid":"39b1d891-1a56-4f7e-b729-12291fd2a9df","position":{"commit_sha":"6e41a12b6ae2713f47f59516c4de0ef8d0ada260","position":"1785397116184812001-39b1d891-1a56-4f7e-b729-12291fd2a9df"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e491c0a5d9bffaef907b077d375a4529c4a3ef8fd785fd42069901e7c78030dc","event_uuid":"ca79f734-043d-4ea7-a5eb-732bfb938fc1","position":{"commit_sha":"7486e0a667f30b6ec5544818674d2a30f1586503","position":"1785397498725000918-ca79f734-043d-4ea7-a5eb-732bfb938fc1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5a0f870e377aedc2443b6413ad5967b6cd8e38af120520387e3d8351fea307f5","event_uuid":"b5156737-b988-4aad-8d2f-8b8a16b14c48","position":{"commit_sha":"f5c53b4fd6ac35f7f6e66b03880e52e7c1e98dba","position":"1785397639487646001-b5156737-b988-4aad-8d2f-8b8a16b14c48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1035. Deviation notes: (1) plan_review/__init__.py sat at 799 LOC against the 800 hard CI cap, so both reuse paths (existing idempotent_reuse + new verdict_reuse) were extracted along the existing call seam into a new plan_review/reuse.py (152 LOC); __init__ now calls reuse.idempotent_reuse / reuse.verdict_reuse. (2) tests placed at tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py (self-contained repo fixture) rather than the plan's tests/llm/ path, which does not exist as a test tier; conventions mirrored from tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_block_loop_remediation.py. 7 new tests green; existing gate/idempotence suites (89 + 47 tests), lint, typecheck all pass locally.","timestamp":1785397639487646001}],"created_at":1785384336307581001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`_idempotent_reuse` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:460-508) requires `claim_gate_check` to pass, which requires a certified signature; a BLOCK never signs (__init__.py:711-717). So re-running review-plan on an unchanged blocked plan re-pays the full ~26-call review. Store history shows 117 unrevised BLOCK retries. The sidecar already stamps `verified_at_sha` on every verdict for exactly this purpose (sidecar.py:600-604: \"a BLOCK loop leaves a usable baseline even though a BLOCK never signs\").\n\n## Approach\nAdd a `_verdict_reuse` path beside `_idempotent_reuse`: when no attestation exists, read `sidecar.latest_review_result`; if its `material_fingerprint` equals `attest.current_material_fingerprint` AND its `verified_at_sha` equals the current review code sha AND its verdict is BLOCK, reconstruct the BLOCK verdict from the stored findings/coaching/coverage and return it with `coverage.llm_ran=False, coverage.verdict_reuse=True`, emitting no new sidecar. `--force` bypasses (existing semantics, _cli/_llm_commands.py:470-477). Precedent for the sidecar-baseline comparison: `attest._sidecar_branch_decision` (attest.py:337-380). Alternative rejected: signing BLOCK attestations — would complicate the claim gate's PASS-only trust model for no claim-side benefit.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (new reuse branch), src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py (render reused BLOCK with a \"reused\" marker; exit 1 preserved), tests/llm/test_plan_review_reuse.py (new).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with FakeRunner: unchanged fingerprint+sha after BLOCK -> zero runner invocations, exit 1; changed fingerprint -> full review runs; --force -> full review runs; PASS idempotent path unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Re-running review-plan on identical material_fingerprint and verified_at_sha after a BLOCK performs zero LLM calls (checked: unit test asserts FakeRunner is never invoked and coverage.verdict_reuse is True).\n- [ ] A reused BLOCK exits 1 and renders the stored findings with a \"reused\" marker (checked: CLI renderer unit test).\n- [ ] --force bypasses verdict reuse and runs the full review (checked: unit test asserts runner invoked).\n- [ ] Existing PASS idempotent-reuse tests pass unmodified (checked: pytest run of the existing reuse tests).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"verdict-reuse branch"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"reused-BLOCK rendering"},{"path":"tests/llm/test_plan_review_reuse.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"5c9b1190-5fa7-47dd-8102-4cb97e636ad2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7e77-cbe5-5bcf-4096","ticket_type":"bug","title":"review-plan re-runs the full LLM review after an unchanged BLOCK (idempotent skip covers PASS only)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["71816f8a-4fed-45ca-a8ba-d34860946ce8","858c1b36-7fa0-44a6-bc5a-cb9fde97cfc2","5c9b1190-5fa7-47dd-8102-4cb97e636ad2","39b1d891-1a56-4f7e-b729-12291fd2a9df","ca79f734-043d-4ea7-a5eb-732bfb938fc1","b5156737-b988-4aad-8d2f-8b8a16b14c48"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785397639487646002,"uuid":"29201d4d-d0c5-486b-a397-63934b28920b"}